.TH "HED-YAZI" "1" "2026-08-20" "hed v1.21.1" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed\-yazi \- Launch the yazi file manager as a chooser.
Selected paths come back as new buffers in hed.
.PP
Launch the \c
.UR https://yazi-rs.github.io/
\f[CR]yazi\f[R]
.UE \c
\ file manager as a chooser.
Selected paths come back as new buffers in hed.
.SH What happens
\f[CR]:yazi\f[R] (also bound to \f[CR]<space>fy\f[R] in the default
leader map):
.IP "1." 3
Build a temp chooser\-file path under \f[CR]$TMPDIR\f[R] (or
\f[CR]/tmp\f[R]).
.IP "2." 3
Hand the terminal off to yazi via the same TUI handoff helper used by
\f[CR]:git\f[R]/lazygit \[em] raw mode is suspended while yazi owns the
screen, restored on exit.
.IP "3." 3
yazi runs as \f[CR]yazi \-\-chooser\-file=<tmp> [start_dir]\f[R].
The user selects one or more entries and presses Enter.
.IP "4." 3
After yazi exits, the chooser file (one absolute path per selected
entry, newline\-terminated) is read back.
Every non\-empty line is opened in hed via
\f[CR]buf_open_or_switch\f[R].
.PP
If the user quits yazi without selecting (\f[CR]q\f[R]), the chooser
file is empty and nothing opens.
.SH Commands
.IP
.EX
:yazi              open at cwd
:yazi <path>       open at <path>
.EE
.SH Dependencies
\f[CR]yazi\f[R] on \f[CR]$PATH\f[R].
See https://yazi\-rs.github.io/ for install.
.SH Notes
.IP \[bu] 2
Multiple\-select is supported \[em] yazi writes one path per line and
hed opens all of them.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]start_dir\f[R] defaults to the editor\[cq]s logical cwd
(\f[CR]E.cwd\f[R]), not the cwd of the focused buffer.
If you want to browse from the current buffer\[cq]s directory, pass it
explicitly: \f[CR]:yazi <C\-r>%\f[R] (or whatever your keymap exposes
for \[lq]current file path\[rq]).
.IP \[bu] 2
The chooser file is always cleaned up after yazi exits, even on error.
